A table @from another, but the database has the new one already (made by
hand, or by a branch): the old table would be dropped and nothing filled.
Refused.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 table menu
-- @from 1 table meal = menu
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `meal` is in the database already: it is not made `@from table` `menu`, and `menu`'s rows would go
